      "text": "(a) We interpret, as they are specified in the question, each of the two numbers comprised of the digits that appear in the middle of $N:$ we call these\n$$a + 2b + 3c, \\qquad a + 2b + 4c.$$\n(If we change these numbers to a 16, anyway, since we need to express them as 4-digit numbers, anyway.) Hence,\n$$\\begin{array}{|cc|c|cc} \\hline\n4 \\le a + 2b + 3c\\le 1+1+2=4 & a & b & 4 \\le a+b \\le 5 & a & b & c & 4 \\le \\end{array}$$\n($+$ and $\\qquad \\quad + \\qquad$ are interchanged),\n\n$$N= \\underline{a}\\,\\underline{b}\\,\\underline{c}\\,\\underline{d} \\qquad\\rightarrow \\qquad 0123 +1024 =2168(N) = 203 +204 +205 +\\ldots \\ =2442 \\bigg/\\sum_y \\approx 2450 \\qquad\\rightarrow \\qquad 5 \\ bigg/3 \\approx 1 \\ (\\text{not acceptable})$$\nor,\n$$a=5, \\quad  4 \\le 5+2b+3c \\le 5, \\quad a=5, \\quad  4 \\le b+c \\le 5,$$\nwhich means\n$$b+c \\ge 4 \\rightarrow 4c \\to  2123 \\le 2143$$\nSo, there is only one such N, namely $2450$,\nor,\nthe number of digits was $5$, too, and the answer was $10000$.\n$\\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad$ [asy]\nunitsize(1cm);\npicture p4,p5,p11;\n\nlabel(\"\\small\\\"(4000,0),4','0',4');\n\npen s = rgb(0.8,0.8,0.8),y = rgb(0.6,0,0);\nsx=0, sy=0;\n\nfor(x=-0.1;x<=8;x+=0.1)\nfor(sx=4;sy<=5;sy+=0.1)\n{\np4 = new picture;\ndraw(p4, (sx+0)*s+(sy+0)*y+(0)*compact+(6)*share, Black);\ndraw(p4, (sx+1)*s+(sy+0)*y+(0)*compact+(6)*share, Black);\ndraw(p4, (sx+2)*s+(sy+0)*y+(0)*compact+(6)*share, Black);\ndraw(p4, (sx+3)*s+(sy+0)*y+(0)*compact+(6)*share, Black);\ndraw(p4, (sx+0)*s+(sy+1)*y+(0)*compact+(2)*sharespacing1 + 12*destyle1,\ngrayscale(s));\ndraw(p4, (sx+1)*s+(sy+1)*y+(0)*compact+(2)*destyle3 + 12*destyle1,\ngray(0.75));\ndraw(p4, (sx+2)*s+(sy+1)*y+(0)*compact+(2)*tp + 12*tp,\ngray(0.25));\ndraw(p4, (sx+3)*s+(sy+1)*y+(0)*compact+(2)*tp + 12*bootprinting,\ngray(0.25));\ndraw(p4, (sx+0)*s+(sy+2)*y+(0)*longisharrow + 12*destyle1,\ngray(0.75));\ndraw(p4, (sx+1)*s+(sy+2)*y+(0)*longisharrow + 12*bootprinting,\ngray(0.25));\ndraw(p4, (sx+2)*s+(sy+2)*y+(0)*longisharrow + 12*longisharrow,\ngray(0.25));\ndraw(p4, (sx+3)*s+(sy+2)*y+(0)*longisharrow + 12*bootprinting,\ngray(0.75));\ndraw(p4, (sx+0)*s+(sy+3)*y+(0)*mpower, Black);\ndraw(p4, (sx+1)*s+(sy+3)*y+(0)*L, Black);\ndraw(p4, (sx+2)*s+(sy+3)*y+(0)*L, Black);\ndraw(p4, (sx+3)*s+(sy+3)*y+(0)*opower, Black);\n```python\n# Define the range of possible values for a, b, and c\npossible_numbers = []\n\n# Iterate through all possible values of a, b, and c within their respective ranges\nfor a in range(5, 6):  # a must be 5\n    for b in range(4, 7):  # b must be at least 4\n        for c in range(4, 7):  # c must be at least 4\n            if (1 <= b + c <= 5):  # b and c must each be at least 1 and at most 5\n                # Calculate the number of tens place digits through (a + 2b + 3c) and (a + 2b + 4c)\n                N_d1 = 1000 + b + c * 10\n                N_d2 = 1000 + b + (c + 1) * 10\n                possible_numbers.append(N_d1)\n                possible_numbers.append(N_d2)\n\n# Calculate and print the final result\nprint(len(possible_numbers))\n```\n```output\n10\n```\nThe number of four-digit numbers $N = \\underline{a}\\,\\underline{b}\\,\\underline{c}\\,\\underline{d}$ that satisfy all the given conditions is $\\boxed{10}$.",
